WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.009
Film Courage: How do you feel on those days
when you have no time to work on your writing?

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:07.540
West Liang: I get really depressed.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.600
I get depressed…I get self-defeating.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:22.900
I’ve always believed about the parable of
the Tortoise and the Hare.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.190
I feel like I’m like the tortoise (kind
of).

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:35.780
I have a really strong, present work ethic,
that sometimes gets really annoying.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.659
So I have a really bad guilty conscious about
not working.

00:00:39.659 --> 00:00:48.870
So there are certain days where I am not doing
any writing or not doing any workshopping

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:55.050
and it’s frustrating because you feel like
you’re not productive.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:01:08.000
But I think going back to a bigger kind of
frame, I think those moments are important

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.180
when I do experience writer’s block.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:17.549
I go for a hike and zone out and I spend a
day at the beach or I am watching a movie

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:19.020
or something.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.619
I think a lot of good can come from that.

00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:27.280
It gives you perspective and distance from
the project a little bit and I also think

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:37.000
if you are not writing because there is something
wrong with the script (the story) or that

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.420
something else is supposed to happen that
you have to think whether it is life things

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:41.479
or whether it’s whatever.

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:45.810
So I try not to beat myself up too much about
it.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.829
But I can be very hard on myself, for sure.

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:50.119
Film Courage: Really…that’s interesting.

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:55.380
I see that you’d be more easy on yourself.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:03.049
West Liang: What we are in this business (so
many of us) we’re not treated as business

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:06.299
owners, we’re not treated as entrepreneurs.

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:09.940
We treated as struggling artists.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:12.080
But we are business owners.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:21.530
We each are running our own business with
limited staff, with high overhead, with trying

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:26.420
to figure out how to make our product different
from competitors.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:30.720
And we’re all struggling to find funding.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.460
We have to kind of wear that hat with a little
more pride.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.440
We are business owners and entrepreneurs.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:48.840
And so it is tough for people because you
feel like you’re not going to work on that

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:49.840
one day.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:50.840
You feel like “Oh no.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:55.170
What’s going on?”

00:02:55.170 --> 00:03:00.190
I think it’s tough when I feel like I am
not being productive.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:06.221
Film Courage: Do you recognize that when you’re
in the moment of that [feeling]?

00:03:06.221 --> 00:03:10.270
Let’s suppose you have a week coming up
where you’re really not going to have time.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:13.810
And you know that and you’re like “Okay…I’m
just going to bite the bullet and do what

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:14.850
I am going to have to do.”

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:19.160
Do you start to recognize it in yourself and
go “Oh, gosh…you know what it is [why

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.160
I feel so badly]?

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.160
It’s because I’m not working on my creative
stuff.”

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:27.900
West Liang: I’ve read a lot of blogs and
watched a lot of interviews with other writers

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:37.070
who either have the luxury to write every
single day because they are being paid to

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:41.820
write a certain script or that’s how they
work.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:50.700
But I think for me, I’m not sure I’m the
kind of writer who writes every day.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.970
Maybe I need to be a little bit better about
that.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:04:04.450
But I try to be mindful of what is inspiring
to me at the moment and letting that energy

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:09.940
build up so I’m not just sitting at a computer
staring at a blank page.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:15.730
For me I think sometimes it’s important
to stare at a blank page and other times it’s

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:27.290
really important to just let that energy build
up, build up, and build up so that 

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:31.390
you have a lot to say and to express and you
put it all on the page.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.620
I think that is important.

